package hartland

model cn

// CN-P6 S6.1 (= AU-hartland P5 S5.1) — the Hartland conceptual package: design `11` §1 on the estate's real names,
// re-modelled at CN-P8 S8.3 (design `14` §4, grammar 0.20): things in time. An EVENT is an instant of the stream; what
// exists with a lifetime or a validity, or relates things, is a KIND (a relator when it `involves:`); what an individual
// is from birth is a SUBKIND; what it enters and leaves is a PHASE (phases.ttrm). No durative event remains.
// The kinds, the role and the events here; their qualities in qualities.ttrm, the recipe vocabulary in phases.ttrm,
// what the `grounds:` sugar cannot say (a relator's or an event's participant paths and period) in
// model/binding/cn.ttrm, the words in model/lexicon/{cs,en}/cn.ttrm.
//
// One grounding per concept (CN-D12). Analytical things ground to md and reach er through the DERIVED hop — hartland
// authors no md2er: md2db and er2db meet on the same table (md/hop HP-P2; design `11` §5, A-H-5). The recipe world
// grounds to er directly, the AU extension's entities (model/er/orders.ttrm, returns-flow.ttrm).
//
// A concept's `label:` is not a lexicon term — the archive holds a concept's TERMS only (lexicon/cn.ttrm). So nothing
// below claims a word; the guards on the estate's words (model/lexicon/tests, lexicon/tests) stay where they are.
//
// No `Party` kind: `Customer` has no base (Q16-5 — add one when a second role of a party appears, a supplier).

// ---- kinds ----
def kind Item         { label: { en: "Product", cs: "Produkt" },                         grounds: md.Product }             // hop → er.entity.item
def kind Store        { label: { en: "Store", cs: "Prodejna" },                          grounds: md.Store }               // hop → er.entity.store
def kind Warehouse    { label: { en: "Distribution center", cs: "Distribuční centrum" }, grounds: md.DistributionCentre }  // hop → er.entity.warehouse
def kind ReturnReason { label: { en: "Return reason", cs: "Důvod reklamace" },           grounds: md.ReturnReason }        // hop → er.entity.reason
// A value kind (AM-27, L16-4): its members are the values of one attribute — store · web · marketplace.
def kind Channel      { label: { en: "Channel", cs: "Kanál" },                           grounds: er.entity.sales.channel }
// The documents: abstract, no rows of its own (an invoice is one from issue to archive — a variant, not a phase).
def kind Document     { label: { en: "Document", cs: "Doklad" }, abstract: true }

// ---- roles ----
// A role's defining event must be an event (CN-D6): `Order` is a kind now, so a customer is who places one.
def role Customer {
    label: { en: "Customer", cs: "Zákazník" },
    event: OrderPlaced,
    grounds: md.Customer                                                         // hop → er.entity.customer
}

// ---- events: the analytical ones (md cubelets behind them) — instants ----
// The three channel cubelets are variants of one event (L16-5, phases.ttrm); `Sale` is the stacked `sales` entity
// over the channel union (md/hop HP-H, A-CN-100) — one grain for "revenue by channel".
def event Sale {
    label: { en: "Sale", cs: "Prodej" },
    involves: [Customer, Item, Channel],
    period: { at: sold_date },
    qualities: [revenue, quantity, sold_date]
}
// The analytical return — the three returns cubelets, on the stacked `channel_returns` entity over their union
// (Q16-2, model/er/channel_returns.ttrm). Not the return REQUEST of the recipe world (`ReturnRequest` below).
def event Return {
    label: { en: "Return", cs: "Vratka" },
    involves: [Customer, Item, ReturnReason],
    period: { at: returned_date },
    qualities: [return_amount, returned_quantity, returned_date]
}
// A reading is an instantaneous measuring (`08b` §5).
def event Inventory {
    label: { en: "Stock reading", cs: "Stav zásob" },
    involves: [Item, Warehouse],
    period: { at: as_of_date },
    qualities: [quantity_on_hand, as_of_date]
}

// ---- kinds: the recipe world (the AU extension) — relators, the rows that relate things ----
// No period: an order's lifecycle is the phase `OpenOrder`, bounded by its two events.
def kind Order {
    label: { en: "Order", cs: "Objednávka" },
    involves: [Customer, Warehouse as fulfilling],
    qualities: [order_value, state, held_for, channel, placed_date, delivered_date]
}
// The sale EVENT is `Sale` (the cubelet grain); a line is the row an order holds.
def kind OrderLine {
    label: { en: "Order line", cs: "Řádek objednávky" },
    involves: [Order, Customer, Item, Warehouse],
    qualities: [line_quantity, unit_price, line_value, line_date]
}
// `14` §4: the act `Invoicing` became the document and its issue; its states are phases (phases.ttrm).
def variant Invoice {
    of: Document,
    label: { en: "Invoice", cs: "Faktura" },
    involves: [Customer, Order],
    qualities: [amount, paid, invoice_status, issued, due]
}
// A, the object with validity (`14` §3) — the row shape of `price_list` / `customer_price`. Their valued-state
// projections (B) are `channel_price` / `agreed_price` (qualities.ttrm). `Channel` is a column of the row (AM-27).
def kind ListPrice {
    label: { en: "List price", cs: "Ceníková cena" },
    involves: [Item, Channel],
    period: { start: pl_from, end: pl_to, end_open: open },
    qualities: [pl_price, pl_channel, pl_from, pl_to]
}
def kind PriceAgreement {
    label: { en: "Individual price", cs: "Individuální cena" },
    involves: [Customer, Item],
    period: { start: cp_from, end: cp_to, end_open: open },
    qualities: [cp_price, cp_from, cp_to]
}
def kind ReturnRequest {
    label: { en: "Return request", cs: "Reklamace" },
    involves: [Customer, Order],
    qualities: [request_state, requested_date]
}
// The H-2 key (D-84). The requested variant of an exchange is no participant: `fk_rl_variant` has no relation
// (model/er/relations.ttrm — a second line → item relation would make every line/item join ambiguous).
def kind ReturnLine {
    label: { en: "Return request line", cs: "Řádek reklamace" },
    involves: [ReturnRequest as request, Customer, Item],
    qualities: [return_quantity, return_unit_price, return_reason, requested_resolution, line_state, way]
}

// ---- events: the recipe world's transitions — instants, only where the stream has one ----
// No `InvoicePaid`: the estate has no paid date (`14` §4). `OrderPlaced` names the customer too: it is the role's
// defining event (CN-D6).
def event OrderPlaced     { label: { en: "Order placed", cs: "Zadání objednávky" },  involves: [Order, Customer], period: { at: placed_date } }
def event OrderDelivered  { label: { en: "Order delivered", cs: "Doručení objednávky" }, involves: [Order],      period: { at: delivered_date } }
def event InvoiceIssued   { label: { en: "Invoice issued", cs: "Vystavení faktury" }, involves: [Invoice],       period: { at: issued } }
def event ReturnRequested { label: { en: "Return requested", cs: "Podání reklamace" }, involves: [ReturnRequest], period: { at: requested_date } }

def phase LargeOrder {
    of: Order,
    label: { cs: "Velká objednávka", en: "Large order" },
    sources: ["recipe://hartland.automation/release_order#s1"],
    definition: """order_value > 1000000"""
}
